>> >  X - 3 uncursed daggers
>
>> Use Q to put them in your quiver.  Always have quivered
>> missile weapons no matter your skill level at throwing.
>
> Also: why only 3.  I can't believe that that's all he's seen.

It is puzzling.  For any class that I don't use a bow and hoard arrows,
I don't stop gathering daggers until I have about a dozen.  Then I
keep picking up new daggers to improve my stack.  I pick up regular
daggers and drop an orcish dagger until out of orcish daggers,
pick up elven daggers and drop regular daggers until out of regular
daggers, keep picking up elven daggers until I have a single stack
of about a dozen, maybe name one of the blessed nonstacking ones.
Once I have a large stack of elven daggers I do serious enchanting
on them to have a quiver of death.

So I think the reason is under valuing missile combat.  I'll almost
never die without some stack of missile weapons quivered.  It's
even more valuable than having an alternately wielded weapon.
Under value missile damage, fail to collect daggers, fail to quiver
the stack of daggers.  That's my guess anyways.

>> >  a - an uncursed blindfold
>
>> I think this is better than a towel.
>
> Why?

The stats for blindfold and towel are identical - weight, price, chance,
so to me the only difference is a tiny bit of simplicity -

A blind fold works by "a"pplying it ("P" works but it does not appear
in the list of options).  A towel works by "P"utting it on and does
something different when "a"pplied.  There's a slightly greater typo
risk with a towel accidentally taking off an amulet or ring by
mistake. That doesn't happen very often but almost all of my
characters die to typos.


